// The Docs sections, in the order they appear on the Docs landing grid.
//
// A section is a finite body of material a reader can enter, work through, and finish. The
// grid states how many pages each holds, because "Prompting" says nothing about whether it is
// an afternoon or a reference you dip into, while "Prompting · 14 pages" tells a reader what
// they are agreeing to (KI-WEBSITE-SITE-037).
//
// Counts and first-page links are NOT declared here. They are derived at build time from the
// pages that actually carry the matching `section` binding, so a card cannot claim a number
// the section does not hold. Adding a page to a section directory is the only thing needed to
// change its count. A declared section whose directory holds only its binding file is a
// registered shelf with nothing on it yet: the landing grid skips it until its first page lands.
//
// `slug` is the directory under src/docs/ and the first path segment of every page in it.

